speechtext:
Yes. These were the alternatives for the men:
(a)	Forestry leave for all wishing same;
(b)	Men of suitable rank, age and Pulhems profile for overseas service in another arm to be given opportunity to transfer;
(c)	Veterans of 1914-18 to have' the privilege of transferring to veterans' guard of Canada;
(d)	Coal-mining leave under existing regulations to those eligible;
(e)	Compassionate farm leave under R.O. 3456 to those eligible;
(f)	Any other type of leave without pay and allowances to those eligible, under existing regulations.

War Appropriation-Army

Yes, and for railways. Then it continues:
(g)	Opportunity for trades training to those suitable and selected and transfer to appropriate corps;
(h)	Authority for discharge of personnel whose Pulhems profile was lower than 2 and who were not specially required in the army by reason of technical military or trades qualifications;
(i)	Personnel returning from forestry leave eligible to take advantage of alternatives (a) to (h).
Those were the instructions given.
